      "writtenOn": "2025-09-26T15:04:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am trying to understand this change... How does setting the `ICC_SRE_EL1.SRE` bit - which I thought simply allowed S-EL1 software to access the GIC through the system registers interface - \"prevent the selection of legacy mode\"? And by \"legacy mode\", do we mean GICv3\u0027s compatibility mode with GICv2?\n\nDoes this relate to the following sentence from https://developer.arm.com/documentation/ddi0601/2025-06/AArch64-Registers/ICC-SRE-EL1--Interrupt-Controller-System-Register-Enable-Register--EL1-:\n\n\u003e GICv3 implementations that do not require GICv2 compatibility might choose to make this bit RAO/WI.\n\n?\n\nApologies if this was discussed in another forum, I might have missed it...",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 188,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 189,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "c0e0fbdcdf54bcf151daa5bf42fd45548ee1e774",
