      "writtenOn": "2025-09-29T12:56:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is quite an obscure feature of the GIC and it already caused some long debug sessions.\nIt is described in \u00274.6.1 Interrupt grouping and security\u0027.\n\u003e Secure Group 1 interrupts are treated as Group 0 by a CPU interface if:\n\u003e — The PE does not implement EL3.\n\u003e — ICC_SRE_EL1_S.SRE \u003d\u003d 0.\n\nThere\u0027s an OR relation in the listed conditions.",
      "parentUuid": "bb4cf01e_fc8ed9ff",
